  "packageHashAlgorithm": "SHA512",
  "packageSize": 682575,
  "published": "2026-11-07T17:48:58.437Z",
  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "v5.10.0: signing in with an OpenID Connect provider you declare, and an external sign-in that fails without a 500. MyIdentity:Authentication:ExternalProviders:<name> declares providers that the library registers with fixed defaults (code flow with PKCE, issuer validated, no saved tokens, email_verified required) and validates at startup; the new IMyIdentityAuthenticationService.ProcessExternalResponseAsync runs the Google callback's contract for them, refuses a result issued by another scheme, anchors the account per provider and audits External:<name>. A failed external callback (Google included) now redirects to the login path with error=ExternalLoginFailed instead of throwing; ProcessGoogleResponseAsync refuses a result carrying another scheme's .AuthScheme; the picture claim is kept only as an absolute http(s) URL of up to 2048 characters. The cascaded state of a static render or a prerender now takes, once, the user that authorized the request (a policy that names its own scheme no longer leaves the page drawn as not authorized); circuits are unchanged and an explicit UpdateAuthenticationState wins. Startup refuses a LoginPath, LogoutPath or AccessDeniedPath that starts with // or /\\ or contains a control character, and an extra scope that is not a single OAuth scope; \"already linked\" compares the provider ignoring case, as the anchor does, and the external login's link is written in a scope of its own, outside any transaction or pending changes of yours. GETTING_STARTED documents the least-privilege account of an API key inside a tenant. A class of your own that implements IMyIdentityAuthenticationService gains a member to implement. New dependency: Microsoft.AspNetCore.Authentication.OpenIdConnect. The package validation baseline is 5.9.0. Upgrading from 5.9.0: MyIdentity/UPGRADE.md §54.",
